Hi Tobias,

I'm not quite sure what you are asking here. The default multipleGroup() setup treats each group as completely independent, so the models should be nearly the same as running the data with mirt() on the group subsets (see the attached for an example). There must be something else going on in your R code causing issues, but I can't locate it. Hope this helps though.

Phil

